{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Lau 2026: strip array, w/d = 0.1, below J_max (ZY)",
  "description": "Lau, Chernin, Heri & Zhang, arXiv:2607.24590 (2026): periodic array of emitting strips (width w = 0.1 d, period p = 2 d), confined flow (z-only motion, infinite axial B), injection energy Delta = E_in/eV = 0.01, V0 = 2.5 kV, d = 1 cm. One period of the array is modelled exactly as in the paper (Fig. 1): the strip is centred at y = 0 and the side boundaries y = -p/2, +p/2 are periodic for fields and particles (an isolated strip is the limit p >> d; p/d = 2 is already close to it). The mesh is refined across the strip and in front of the cathode (Mesh Refinement). Steady-state limit, Eq. (7): J_max = 5.197 J_CL (5.193 in the Lau 2026 tutorial; paper test E1 with p = 5.12 d: 5.191). Below J_max: I_anode = Iemit, I_cathode = 0 and the potential minimum (line probe 'phi' along the centre line: depth probe_phi_min and position probe_phi_zmin) stays above -Delta*V0. Above J_max: virtual cathode, phi_min -> -Delta*V0 and part of the current returns to the cathode (I_cathode < 0). Use the sweep over Jn = J/J_CL to locate the limit. Magnetic field: Species > motion = z_only is the infinite axial field (electrons move only along z, the assumption of Luginsland et al. 1996 and Lau 2001); motion = full uses the applied field 'axial B' = [Bz, 0, 0] T with the parameter Bz (0 = no field, or any finite value, e.g. 0.1, 1, 10).",
